import{_ as e,o as a,c as i,a2 as r}from"./chunks/framework.CDpkVv68.js";const m=JSON.parse('{"title":"Three-weapon numeric combat prototype","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/game-design/combat/numeric-prototype.md","filePath":"en/game-design/combat/numeric-prototype.md"}'),n={name:"en/game-design/combat/numeric-prototype.md"};function d(o,t,s,l,c,h){return a(),i("div",null,[...t[0]||(t[0]=[r('<h1 id="three-weapon-numeric-combat-prototype" tabindex="-1">Three-weapon numeric combat prototype <a class="header-anchor" href="#three-weapon-numeric-combat-prototype" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Three-weapon numeric combat prototype&quot;">​</a></h1><p><strong>Design status: Experimental numeric test profile; underlying Modern/Legacy design remains Proposed.</strong> <strong>Implementation/availability:</strong> this profile is not implemented or playable. <strong>Verification:</strong> documentation and arithmetic review only; no game-feel evidence. <strong>Reviewed:</strong> 2026-10-09, Batch 06.</p><p><a href="/Syrolands-Public/en/guide/combat/numeric-prototype.html">Player summary</a> · <a href="/Syrolands-Public/en/game-design/combat/actions.html">Action schema</a> · <a href="/Syrolands-Public/en/game-design/combat/variable-registry.html#batch-06-implementation-triage">Variable triage</a></p><h2 id="scope-and-units" tabindex="-1">Scope and units <a class="header-anchor" href="#scope-and-units" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Scope and units&quot;">​</a></h2><p>This is one deliberately small test profile, not final balance, an implementation authorization or a replacement for the existing combat experiment. It tests spacing, tempo, resource pressure, mode differences, counters and readable reach. Every new number on this page is <strong>Experimental</strong>. Values describe test fixtures, not player progression requirements.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Quantity</th><th>Test representation</th><th>Boundary</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Stamina</td><td>Pool 100; start full</td><td>Independent normalized fixture, not a new stat formula</td></tr><tr><td>Regeneration</td><td>6 units/second after 1000 ms without a paid action; disabled during any action phase</td><td>Same in both modes; no free defense refill</td></tr><tr><td>Time</td><td>Server elapsed milliseconds</td><td>Client animation never authorizes completion</td></tr><tr><td>Reach</td><td>Integer tiles using Chebyshev grid distance; same tile excluded</td><td>LOS and facing still required; not pixel hitboxes</td></tr><tr><td>Accuracy</td><td>Action modifiers in percentage points (pp)</td><td>Equal-skill neutral fixture baseline 75%; clamp final chance 5–95%; not a replacement skill formula</td></tr><tr><td>Damage</td><td>Relative pre-mitigation index D0 = 1.00 for a common neutral reference hit</td><td>No absolute HP, DPS or TTK target; no independent local-trauma multiplier</td></tr><tr><td>Skill/stats</td><td>Equal weapon skill 50, DEX 50 for baseline; DEX 0/100 sensitivity cases</td><td>Fixture controls only; STR/INT held neutral, no new skill/stat formula</td></tr><tr><td>Armor/health</td><td>Hold existing setup constant between trials</td><td>No new HP/integrity totals, armor formula or durability loop</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The relative damage index is for comparison and later calibration. It must not be inserted after mitigation or multiplied into local integrity. Existing <a href="/Syrolands-Public/en/game-design/combat/damage.html">global/local separation and accepted experimental trauma policy</a> retain authority. Cutting, piercing and blunt emphases below are qualitative; fractures, bleeding and penetration arithmetic are not implemented or selected here. Before gameplay implementation, reconcile action damage with the existing authoritative damage pipeline. Until then, evaluate relative outcomes on paper without claiming those numbers are live.</p><h2 id="shared-phase-and-input-rules" tabindex="-1">Shared phase and input rules <a class="header-anchor" href="#shared-phase-and-input-rules" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Shared phase and input rules&quot;">​</a></h2><p>An accepted action pays stamina once at initiation. Insufficient stamina rejects it. Wind-up (W), active window (A), then recovery (R) run in order; no other action starts before all three finish, including defense. “Immediate defense” means an available manual action bypasses the Legacy swing queue, not that it cancels an already committed action. This restriction is itself a test hypothesis.</p><ul><li>Modern starts on a valid input; no automatic swing timer blocks it. Recovery gates follow-up inputs.</li><li>A rejected input causes no damage, stamina charge, buffer or new timer; held input is one intent until released. Count only distinct presses for the spam test below.</li><li>Revalidate target, LOS and footprint at contact. Single-target actions contact once; arcs contact each eligible target at most once per action. Moving away can defeat an initiated strike.</li><li>All actions are interruptible during wind-up by voluntary cancellation or loss of required equipment/actor validity; cost is not refunded and full recovery follows. Ordinary damage alone does not interrupt this initial profile. Losing spatial validity causes a miss, not a refunded cancellation. Death terminates the action under existing lifecycle rules.</li><li>Active phase cannot be voluntarily cancelled. Counter reactions cannot chain from other counters. Counter damage still checks accuracy, range, LOS and armor.</li><li>Walking is allowed except where the weapon table says planted; running cancels wind-up and pays the same recovery. No speed multiplier or new movement system is selected.</li></ul><h2 id="longsword-kit" tabindex="-1">Longsword kit <a class="header-anchor" href="#longsword-kit" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Longsword kit&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Medium commitment, reliable close control. Values assume Practiced, neutral handling and Stable rhythm. Active windows do not grant multiple hits.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Action</th><th>Type / reach</th><th>Stamina</th><th>W / A / R (ms)</th><th>Accuracy</th><th>Relative damage / emphasis</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Basic Slash</td><td>Basic; 1</td><td>10</td><td>250 / 150 / 600</td><td>+0 pp</td><td>1.00; cutting</td></tr><tr><td>Thrust</td><td>Offensive SA; 1</td><td>13</td><td>300 / 100 / 650</td><td>+5 pp</td><td>0.95; precise piercing, armor benefit qualitative only</td></tr><tr><td>Feint</td><td>Deception SA; 1</td><td>7</td><td>250 / 100 / 400</td><td>No hit roll</td><td>0; no contact or automatic debuff</td></tr><tr><td>Riposte</td><td>Defensive SA; 1</td><td>15</td><td>100 / 450 / 650</td><td>+0 pp on counter</td><td>1.05 counter, only after compatible defended contact</td></tr></tbody></table><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Action</th><th>Footprint / effective range</th><th>Telegraph / movement</th><th>Special eligibility and counterplay</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Basic Slash</td><td>Selected target, front 90-degree sector; 1</td><td>Medium; walk</td><td>Ordinary commitment; can miss a retreat</td></tr><tr><td>Thrust</td><td>Selected target on facing grid ray; 1</td><td>Medium, point-forward cue; planted W+A</td><td>Narrower alignment and longer recovery trade for precision</td></tr><tr><td>Feint</td><td>No impact footprint; apparent Slash cue</td><td>Same opening cue as Slash, visible pullback at A; walk</td><td>Does not force a response; a defender may wait, move or attack</td></tr><tr><td>Riposte</td><td>Selected incoming attacker in front sector; 1</td><td>Clear guard posture; planted W+A</td><td>First compatible frontal Basic Slash, Basic Thrust or Basic Swing during A only</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Riposte reduces that compatible incoming pre-mitigation impact index by 25% and attempts one counter at the contact event, paid by its original cost. It is not a free attack button; without a valid defended contact there is no counter and time/stamina are spent. Heavy Blow, Lunge, arcs and Guard Break do not trigger its counter. Required visual contact and actual pipeline integration remain implementation gates.</p><h2 id="spear-kit" tabindex="-1">Spear kit <a class="header-anchor" href="#spear-kit" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Spear kit&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Spacing and approach punishment, with weak close handling. No forward teleport or automatic displacement is part of Lunge.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Action</th><th>Type / reach</th><th>Stamina</th><th>W / A / R (ms)</th><th>Accuracy</th><th>Relative damage / emphasis</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Basic Thrust</td><td>Basic; 2</td><td>12</td><td>350 / 150 / 700</td><td>+0 pp</td><td>1.00; piercing</td></tr><tr><td>Lunge</td><td>Offensive SA; 3</td><td>22</td><td>500 / 150 / 1000</td><td>−5 pp</td><td>1.15; committed piercing</td></tr><tr><td>Brace</td><td>Defensive SA; 2</td><td>18</td><td>150 / 1600 / 850</td><td>+0 pp on counter</td><td>1.10 counter, compatible contact only</td></tr><tr><td>Sweep</td><td>Offensive SA; 1</td><td>20</td><td>450 / 200 / 850</td><td>−10 pp</td><td>0.60 per target, maximum 2; low penetration</td></tr></tbody></table><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Action</th><th>Footprint / effective range</th><th>Telegraph / movement</th><th>Special eligibility and counterplay</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Basic Thrust</td><td>Selected target on facing ray; best 2</td><td>Medium point-forward cue; walk</td><td>At 1 tile: −10 pp additional accuracy, damage index ×0.85</td></tr><tr><td>Lunge</td><td>Selected target on facing ray; best 2–3</td><td>Strong forward-extension cue; planted W+A</td><td>Same 1-tile penalty; no movement until recovery; retreat/flank punishes commitment</td></tr><tr><td>Brace</td><td>Frontal 90-degree sector, selected attacker; best 2</td><td>Clear set-spear posture; planted W+A</td><td>First compatible Basic Slash, Basic Swing, Heavy Blow or Lunge contact during A</td></tr><tr><td>Sweep</td><td>Front 90-degree sector, 1 tile</td><td>Strong low-arc cue; planted W+A</td><td>No knockback/stun; reduced per-target impact tests space control</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Brace reduces compatible incoming pre-mitigation impact by 35% and attempts one counter at the contact event. Its counter at 1 tile takes the same −10 pp and ×0.85 close-range penalties. After triggering, the remaining active time ends and full recovery begins; Riposte uses the same one-trigger rule. Neither stance tracks or turns after activation. Feint, delay until the stance ends, flank, retreat outside counter reach or incompatible attack can defeat it. A failed/missed counter is not retried. The 1600 ms active test replaces the earlier illustrative “about 2 seconds” only for this profile.</p><h2 id="war-hammer-kit" tabindex="-1">War Hammer kit <a class="header-anchor" href="#war-hammer-kit" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;War Hammer kit&quot;">​</a></h2><p>High impact and visible commitment, not a highest-DPS reward. <strong>Guard Break</strong> is chosen over Stun to exercise guard interactions without introducing generic crowd-control duration, immunity and chain-stun rules.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Action</th><th>Type / reach</th><th>Stamina</th><th>W / A / R (ms)</th><th>Accuracy</th><th>Relative damage / emphasis</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Basic Swing</td><td>Basic; 1</td><td>17</td><td>500 / 200 / 1000</td><td>−5 pp</td><td>1.20; blunt impact</td></tr><tr><td>Heavy Blow</td><td>Offensive SA; 1</td><td>28</td><td>750 / 150 / 1400</td><td>−10 pp</td><td>1.50; high local/blunt emphasis, no trauma multiplier</td></tr><tr><td>Crushing Arc</td><td>Offensive SA; 2</td><td>30</td><td>650 / 250 / 1300</td><td>−15 pp</td><td>0.70 per target, maximum 2; blunt area pressure</td></tr><tr><td>Guard Break</td><td>Offensive SA; 1</td><td>24</td><td>600 / 150 / 1100</td><td>−5 pp</td><td>0.90; guard interaction, not armor destruction</td></tr></tbody></table><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Action</th><th>Footprint / effective range</th><th>Telegraph / movement</th><th>Trade-off</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Basic Swing</td><td>Selected target, front 90-degree sector; 1</td><td>Strong swing cue; walk</td><td>Slower and costlier than sword</td></tr><tr><td>Heavy Blow</td><td>Selected target, front sector; 1</td><td>Very strong raised-weapon cue; planted W+A</td><td>Long punishable recovery; compatible with Brace</td></tr><tr><td>Crushing Arc</td><td>Front 90-degree sector; 1–2</td><td>Very strong wide-arc cue; planted W+A</td><td>Low precision, high cost; visible 2-tile reach required</td></tr><tr><td>Guard Break</td><td>Selected target, front sector; 1</td><td>Strong guard-directed cue; planted W+A</td><td>Only halves the reduction granted by active Brace/Riposte for this contact</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Guard Break treats either active frontal stance as eligible for its guard reduction, but does not trigger that stance&#39;s counter. Brace&#39;s 35% becomes 17.5%; Riposte&#39;s 25% becomes 12.5%. No lingering debuff, shield disable, durability damage or armor bypass is added. Existing shield/armor mitigation still applies separately. Without an active qualifying stance, it is simply the 0.90 strike. Shield-specific extension remains deferred.</p><p>For Sweep/Crushing Arc, select at most two valid hostile targets in the footprint at the first active instant: selected target first if eligible, then nearest, stable server identity as tie-break. No ally damage, incidental neutral aggro or extra full-strength secondary hit in this test. Resolve separate hit/mitigation per target, total relative index capped by the listed per-target ×2. Facing locks at initiation for planted actions. Footprints must be displayed before impact; if available assets cannot communicate them, block implementation of the affected action rather than grant invisible reach.</p><h2 id="cadence-and-burst-pressure" tabindex="-1">Cadence and burst pressure <a class="header-anchor" href="#cadence-and-burst-pressure" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Cadence and burst pressure&quot;">​</a></h2><p>For each offensive action define reference rhythm <strong>T = W + A + 1.5 × base R</strong>. Use unmodified table durations: no circular feedback from Flow, Familiarity or chain penalties. A Modern follow-up may start once actual phases finish; compare elapsed time since the previous accepted damaging offensive start to that previous action&#39;s T. First action has no interval and starts Stable. Feint and defensive actions reset the rhythm to Stable with no streak; they cannot farm Flow. Weapon/mode changes and target changes also reset it.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Interval / previous T</th><th>Band</th><th>Stamina multiplier</th><th>Accuracy</th><th>Recovery multiplier</th><th>Rhythm result</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>0.85–1.35 inclusive</td><td>Normal</td><td>×1.00</td><td>+0 pp</td><td>×1.00</td><td>Eligible stable interval</td></tr><tr><td>0.70–less than 0.85</td><td>Slightly rushed</td><td>×1.10</td><td>−2 pp</td><td>×1.05</td><td>Stable; streak cleared</td></tr><tr><td>0.55–less than 0.70</td><td>Rushed</td><td>×1.25</td><td>−5 pp</td><td>×1.15</td><td>Off Rhythm</td></tr><tr><td>Less than 0.55</td><td>Spam</td><td>×1.50</td><td>−10 pp</td><td>×1.25</td><td>Off Rhythm</td></tr><tr><td>Greater than 1.35</td><td>Pause / irregular</td><td>×1.00</td><td>+0 pp</td><td>×1.00</td><td>Stable; streak cleared, no inactivity punishment</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Actual phase gates always win; a band does not grant permission to bypass recovery. Some lower bands are unreachable with neutral actions; retain them for modified recovery and future mixed-action trials, not as extra attack slots. Three distinct unavailable attack presses within 500 ms while committed trigger Off Rhythm, but create no additional attacks. Server receipt time owns this test; latency tolerance, duplicate transport filtering and accessibility require validation before implementation.</p><h2 id="flow-test" tabindex="-1">Flow test <a class="header-anchor" href="#flow-test" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Flow test&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Only Modern uses Flow. Start Stable. Three consecutive Normal accepted intervals enter Flow <strong>for the next action</strong>, not retroactively. A rushed/Spam interval or the repeated rejected-input pattern enters Off Rhythm immediately for the triggering accepted action (or the next accepted action after rejected inputs). Three Normal intervals restore Stable; a further three enter Flow. Slightly rushed intervals reset the streak. Strong irregularity also enters Off Rhythm: two consecutive non-pause interval ratios that differ by more than 0.50 (for example 0.75 then 1.30). This is a broad change-of-tempo test, not a perfect-beat requirement. A pause above 1.35T clears Flow to Stable, but does not clear Off Rhythm until either three Normal intervals or 3000 ms without an accepted or rejected attack input. After that idle timeout reset Stable. No exact BPM or narrow perfect-hit window is required.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>State</th><th>Stamina</th><th>Recovery</th><th>Accuracy</th><th>Consistency</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Off Rhythm</td><td>×1.05</td><td>×1.05</td><td>+0 pp</td><td>Reduced (qualitative feedback only)</td></tr><tr><td>Stable</td><td>×1.00</td><td>×1.00</td><td>+0 pp</td><td>Standard</td></tr><tr><td>Flow</td><td>×0.95</td><td>×0.95</td><td>+0 pp</td><td>Refined (qualitative feedback only)</td></tr></tbody></table><p>An action outside Normal loses existing Flow before cost calculation. A Normal interval completing entry still uses the old state; the next Normal action receives Flow benefits. Other candidate fixed/adaptive/personal timing models remain alternatives, not parallel active rules. Consistency changes no random damage distribution in this first profile.</p><p>For accepted actions: cost = base cost × Familiarity × chain × rhythm; recovery = base R × Familiarity × chain × rhythm. Round cost upward to whole units and recovery upward to 10 ms; clamp total cost multiplier to 0.80–1.80 and recovery to 0.85–1.60. W is unchanged; stance active tolerance is defined below. Accuracy = fixture 75% + action pp + range pp + Familiarity pp + chain pp, clamped 5–95%. Apply Familiarity only to learned SAs; basics use Practiced neutral factors. No hidden mode damage modifier. Feint/defense use chain ×1 and Stable rhythm economics; they reset Flow on acceptance.</p><p>Example: Practiced Longsword Basic Slash has T=1300 ms and 1000 ms minimum phase duration. Starting the next Slash at 1000 ms is Slightly rushed (0.769): cost 11, R=630 ms. Waiting 1200 ms is Normal: cost 10, R=600 ms, or cost 10 after upward rounding and R=570 ms while already in Flow. Stable spear basic T=1550 ms, hammer basic T=2200 ms.</p><h2 id="legacy-test" tabindex="-1">Legacy test <a class="header-anchor" href="#legacy-test" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Legacy test&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Legacy schedules the next offensive initiation from the previous offensive start using that action&#39;s T (including an offensive SA or Feint); it never starts before actual recovery ends. Initial target selection waits one basic interval. Invalid target/range conditions delay a swing, never accumulate catch-up swings. When validity returns and the due time has passed, start one action and reschedule from that start. A queued learned/prepared offensive SA replaces one basic action; it is not an extra swing. Empty queue uses the basic. Defense is manual and may start only when phases permit; it cancels the queued offense and schedules the next basic opportunity one interval after defense recovery.</p><p><strong>Interval = T × clamp((1 + 0.15 × (1 − stamina/100)) × handling × dexFactor, 0.90, 1.20).</strong> Sample stamina before paying the outgoing action. dexFactor = 1 − 0.05 × clamp((DEX − 50)/50, −1, 1). Handling is fixed neutral 1.00 initially, with isolated 0.97/1.03 sensitivity trials; no equipment-quality mapping is selected. Fatigue is derived from stamina here, not another meter. Round interval upward to 10 ms. DEX affects this schedule only, not wind-up/accuracy/damage. STR/INT have no profile modifier.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Weapon basic</th><th>Full stamina / DEX 50 / handling 1</th><th>Full stamina, DEX 0–100, handling 1</th><th>Global clamp limits</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Longsword</td><td>1300 ms</td><td>1370–1240 ms</td><td>1170–1560 ms</td></tr><tr><td>Spear</td><td>1550 ms</td><td>1630–1480 ms</td><td>1400–1860 ms</td></tr><tr><td>War Hammer</td><td>2200 ms</td><td>2310–2090 ms</td><td>1980–2640 ms</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Legacy pays the same base/Familiarity costs and phases. It has neither Flow benefits nor rush-band penalties on automatic swings. This is explicit, not a secret mode bonus; compare sustain and missed opportunities in playtests. Bounded DEX and the 1.20 ceiling prevent low-DEX slow motion. Equal base numbers do not establish equal outcomes.</p><h2 id="familiarity-test-and-prepared-sas" tabindex="-1">Familiarity test and prepared SAs <a class="header-anchor" href="#familiarity-test-and-prepared-sas" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Familiarity test and prepared SAs&quot;">​</a></h2><p>For martial SAs only in this slice; spell-pattern tier names are shared but these numbers do not assign spell cast times, mana, fizzle or reference delays. Basic attacks remain neutral. No raw damage modifier.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Tier</th><th>Stamina</th><th>Recovery</th><th>Accuracy</th><th>Defensive active tolerance</th><th>Telegraph / consistency</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Learned</td><td>×1.05</td><td>×1.05</td><td>−2 pp</td><td>×0.95</td><td>Obvious / less refined</td></tr><tr><td>Practiced</td><td>×1.00</td><td>×1.00</td><td>+0 pp</td><td>×1.00</td><td>Standard / standard</td></tr><tr><td>Mastered</td><td>×0.97</td><td>×0.97</td><td>+1 pp</td><td>×1.05</td><td>Refined / steadier; still readable</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Round defensive active tolerance to nearest 10 ms, ties upward (Riposte 430/450/470; Brace 1520/1600/1680). Other active windows and all wind-ups remain unchanged. Telegraph refinement changes cue quality only: no invisible cue, delayed cue start or Tactics threshold selected. No extra success RNG for activating a valid SA.</p><p>Known SAs remain permanently learned. Prepare up to <strong>5</strong>, one slot per SA, no INT scaling. Basics use no slot. Require appropriate weapon, learned knowledge and preparation at initiation. Allow loadout changes only with no selected hostile target, no active/queued action and no hostile action dealt or received for 10 seconds. Changing mode/weapon clears queued SAs and rhythm but never shortens running phases; changes take effect only after recovery. Future INT/preparation complexity effects remain unresolved.</p><h3 id="maintenance-test" tabindex="-1">Maintenance test <a class="header-anchor" href="#maintenance-test" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Maintenance test&quot;">​</a></h3><p>An active day is a UTC date with at least 10 minutes of logged-in, non-idle character activity; a qualifying world or training session may count only after that threshold. This is a provisional accounting convention, not a selected anti-bot detector. Store the last seven such days; calendar absence adds no days and causes no decay. Starting a test character at a chosen tier is fixture setup, not a progression shortcut.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Retain tier</th><th>Qualifying world uses in rolling 7 active days</th><th>Or dedicated training repetitions in same window</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Mastered</td><td>20</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td>Practiced</td><td>9</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>Learned</td><td>No requirement</td><td>Permanent floor</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Count per technique. Evaluate once at completion of each active day, only after seven active days have accrued since learning/tier gain. If the current tier&#39;s threshold fails, lose at most one tier per evaluation; never lose knowledge. Either column independently meets the threshold; no mixed-use exchange ratio yet. Tier gains are still unresolved; this is retention only. Prepared techniques get no slower decay in this first test. A world use must be a valid, stamina-paid attempt against a meaningful non-cooperative challenge; hit success is not required. A training repetition must finish a prescribed facility exercise, not merely click a dummy. Threat eligibility, idling, collusion, repeated-target caps and automation controls remain implementation blockers. Facilities maintain fluency, not optimal core-skill gain or free discovery. Spell maintenance can test the same count convention later, but spell effects are outside this slice.</p><h2 id="evaluation-and-unresolved-gates" tabindex="-1">Evaluation and unresolved gates <a class="header-anchor" href="#evaluation-and-unresolved-gates" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Evaluation and unresolved gates&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Compare modes with identical fixtures, then change one input at a time: neutral versus low stamina; DEX 0/50/100; close versus ideal reach; Learned/Practiced/Mastered; regular versus rushed; successful versus baited defense. Record accepted/rejected inputs, elapsed phase times, stamina, spacing misses, counter attempts and player readability. No numeric success target is established by these paper values.</p><p>Unresolved before gameplay work: actual asset reach and facing, authoritative contact/area integration, how relative damage joins existing mitigation/trauma, existing shield composition, transport/latency tolerance, key mapping/accessibility, hostile-target filtering, stamina fixture compatibility, qualifying activity and exploit controls. No new HP/TTK, armor penetration formula, injury type, spell number, stun, item wear or persistent schema. Archery retains no mandatory basic timing minigame, player-controlled Modern release/aim, automatic Legacy release and optional shared SA timing challenges; bows receive no numeric kit here.</p>',53)])])}const u=e(n,[["render",d]]);export{m as __pageData,u as default};
